0..77 Comment "// The circle and the integers without a higher inductive type. The circle is"
78..153 Comment "// presented by a point, a loop and its inverse, with the two cancellations"
154..228 Comment "// as rules; its shape is a signature. The integers are presented the same"
229..303 Comment "// way, so they model the shape with laws that are conversion: the winding"
304..379 Comment "// number folds the circle into them, and spinning folds them back, and the"
380..457 Comment "// two are an equivalence whose round trips are proved by induction over each"
458..535 Comment "// presented type. A model over the native integers stands beside it with its"
536..610 Comment "// laws owed, and the winding number into it is a fold that rests on those"
611..619 Comment "// laws."
621..698 Comment "/// The circle as a presented type: its rules rewrite constructor terms, so a"
699..741 Comment "/// word normalizes to the loops it winds."
742..744 Other "@["
