7620..7693 Comment "/// The winding number into the native integers, a fold that rests on the"
7694..7751 Comment "/// native model\'s laws. At `Loop(Unloop(x))` it computes"
7752..7823 Comment "/// `turn(unturn(native_wind(x)))`, which conversion does not reduce to"
7824..7900 Comment "/// `native_wind(x)` on a variable; the law `turnUnturn` states exactly that"
7901..7977 Comment "/// path, so `respects` names it for the first rule and `unturnTurn` for the"
7978..8052 Comment "/// second. The loop arms call the model\'s operations rather than spelling"
8053..8131 Comment "/// `n + 1`, so each side the rule relates is the law\'s own endpoint. The fold"
8132..8174 Comment "/// checks and owes what its two laws owe."
